  "stage_3_rescore": "The run itself scored stage 3 fail with the harness at a207aff: it judged dry run 101 (version 5), which the kernel required after the owner's edits to the enabled playbook and which rightly saw both PRs as already run. #166 makes stage 3 judge the latest dry run before the first poll run; re-scored from the run's own run_start, stage 3 judges dry run 94 (version 2: both PRs would run, #3 reviewed, nothing recorded) and passes. Every other stage scored the same in both summaries.",
  "findings_fixed_on_the_way": [
    "First live run (run start 2026-10-29T12:23:09Z, sandbox PRs #1/#2, not counted): Wright made itself the duty's owner. Root cause: memory/wright/role.md is written once and never rewritten, and the installed copy predated the crew and duty guidance. Guidance order fixed in vikashruhilgit/loomwright-studio#164; the runbook's setup now checks role.md. Still open: nothing tells the owner when a shipped template changes (docs/OPEN_QUESTIONS.md).",
    "Stage 3 judged the first done dry run (#163), then the latest of the current version (#166 corrects it to the latest before the first poll, and adds STUDIO_LIVE_RUN_START_FROM to re-score a run).",
    "Wright's first reviewer charter in this run (approval 13, denied) lacked the kernel GitHub read tools and named a guessed workspace; an agent with the github grant has every gh call denied, so it could not have read a PR. Guidance fixed in #165.",
    "Wright's post-approval playbook draft proposed a 15-minute interval though the owner's sentence said 2 minutes, and a 200,000 daily token limit while one dry run used about 101,500; the owner had Wright change the interval (version 2). Not yet an item: the session woken by an approval may not see the owner's original sentence (unverified).",
    "The owner's first Set edits did not register until the Set button was pressed; an edit to the enabled playbook made it a draft again, needing a new dry run and enable (by design: a changed playbook is reviewed before it runs)."
